{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/14/codegen_prompts/7.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/14`\n- 题号：`7`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/14/7.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"7\">\n- `description`：识别网格中每个封闭围栏内的\"种子\"像素颜色，用该颜色按照围栏形状的缺口方向向外进行洪水填充，直到碰到另一个围栏或网格边界。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干由灰色像素构成的近似封闭矩形围栏（一像素宽的边框），每个围栏的四条边中恰好有一条边存在一个单像素宽的缺口。每个围栏内部有且仅有一个非黑色、非灰色的彩色\"种子\"像素。不同围栏内的种子颜色各不相同。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个围栏，找到其边框上的缺口位置，确定缺口朝向的方向（上、下、左、右）。\n  - 从缺口位置开始，沿缺口朝外的方向，用围栏内种子像素的颜色对黑色背景区域进行填充：沿该方向绘制一条与围栏缺口所在边等宽的色带，持续延伸直到遇到另一个围栏的灰色边框像素或到达网格边界。\n  - 围栏本身（灰色边框）保持不变，围栏内部除种子像素外保持黑色，种子像素也保持原色。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要完成两步非显然推理：第一步是发现每个围栏上的缺口位置决定了填充方向（缺口是\"出口\"），第二步是理解填充区域的宽度不是单像素射线，而是与缺口所在边的围栏内部宽度相同的色带，且填充终止于其他围栏的阻挡。种子像素的角色是提供颜色而非位置。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/8b7bacbf, train/ac6f9922, train/aa62e3f4, train/6ca952ad, eval/b9e38dc0, train/df9fd884, train/5adee1b2, eval/dbff022c\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4504\nmechanism=0.5113\nlexical=0.0134\ncode_feature=0.8333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:ray_loop, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:marker, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:flood_fill, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8b7bacbf.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Find single pixels on grid edges that are endpoints of lines, trace along the line to find connected closed regions, and fill those regions with the edge pixel's color.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"single colored pixels s on grid edge that are endpoints of a line\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed regions d connected to the line\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d is reachable by following the line from s\",\n  \"path\": \"trace along the continuous line from edge pixel s\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill interior of each closed region d encountered along path with s.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"d.interior.color = s.color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify single pixels on grid edge; Step 2: trace the line connected to each edge pixel; Step 3: for each closed region touching the line, flood-fill its interior with edge pixel color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"path-tracing\",\n    \"edge-detection\",\n    \"region-filling\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ac6f9922\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4175\nmechanism=0.5218\nlexical=0.0132\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:closed_region, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/ac6f9922.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/ac6f9922.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSummarize the enclosed table slots by the single object color inside each slot, using the slot background color for empty slots.\n\nInput structure\n- The most common color forms the outer background and all enclosed slot\n  backgrounds.\n- The enclosed background components form a complete rectangular array of\n  slots, ordered by their positions.\n- Each slot contains either no other color or exactly one object color.\n\nRule\n- Find all 4-connected components of the most common color that do not touch\n  the input edge.\n- Sort their bounding boxes into row and column order to define the output\n  table.\n- For each slot, output its unique non-background color if present; otherwise\n  output the background color.\n\nKey insight\n- The large grid is an expanded table: the enclosed background components are\n  the cells, and any colored object drawn inside a cell is that cell's summary\n  value.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"enclosed 4-connected background-color slot components arranged as a rectangular table, each containing zero or one non-background object color\",\n  \"transform\": \"collapse each slot to one output pixel in row/column order: use the contained object color if present, otherwise use the background color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"number of slot rows x number of slot columns\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"aa62e3f4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3813\nmechanism=0.4094\nlexical=0.0145\ncode_feature=0.8333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:ray_loop, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/aa62e3f4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/aa62e3f4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReplace the outlined object with the outside contour of that outline in the marker color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background surrounds one 8-connected foreground outline.\n- The outline is the unique largest foreground color.\n- One or more smaller interior colors are inside the outline; the marker color\n  is the unique smallest non-outline color.\n\nRule:\n- Erase all original foreground pixels to background.\n- Paint every background pixel that is 4-adjacent to the outline with the\n  marker color.\n- Keep the grid shape unchanged.\n\nKey insight: The colored interior marker supplies the paint color, while the\nlargest outline supplies only the contour whose outside edge is traced.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"one 8-connected largest foreground outline object and smaller interior marker colors on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase all original foreground pixels; repaint the background pixels 4-adjacent to the outline with the unique smallest non-outline marker color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6ca952ad\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3900\nmechanism=0.4814\nlexical=0.0133\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:hole, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6ca952ad.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/6ca952ad.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDrop every large foreground object straight down to the bottom while leaving small marker objects fixed.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a dominant background color and exactly one foreground color.\n- The foreground is split into separated 4-connected objects.\n- Objects of area at most three are stationary markers; larger objects are moving sprites.\n\nRule:\n- Clear each moving sprite from its original position.\n- Translate each moving sprite vertically downward until its bbox bottom reaches the grid bottom.\n- Repaint each translated sprite in its original color; small markers stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- Object area separates the active falling sprites from the small fixed markers, and all active sprites follow the same vertical path.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected foreground objects with area greater than three pixels\",\n  \"path\": \"vertical downward ray in the object's original columns until its bbox bottom touches the grid bottom\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"translate the whole object once without changing shape or color\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear moved objects at their original positions; leave foreground objects of area at most three pixels fixed\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"b9e38dc0\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4217\nmechanism=0.5156\nlexical=0.0127\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:flood_fill, operation:ray_cast, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/b9e38dc0.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/b9e38dc0.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill the region enclosed by a wall sprite and radiate color outward through its opening.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Wall = most frequent non-bg color, forming a partial enclosure (e.g. U-shape).\n- A fill-color pixel sits inside the enclosed area. Other non-bg pixels may act as obstacles.\nRule:\n- Flood-fill the enclosed area with the fill color, radiating outward through the wall's open end.\n- Obstacles cast \"shadows\" along the radiate direction, blocking fill behind them.\n\nKey insight: The wall endpoints define the opening direction; fill radiates outward through it, and obstacles block propagation along that same axis.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"A pixel inside a half-surrounded area fills and radiates outward along the border opening, while isolated pixels move to grid edge in the radiate direction, leaving background trail\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"innermost connected same-color pixel s inside the half-surrounded inner area of a sprite\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"fill the surrounded area and radiate along the surrounded border opening\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"flood_fill\",\n    \"ray_casting\",\n    \"path_extension\",\n    \"obstacle\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"In the second transformation, the sprite s acts as an obstacle blocking the path of s2\",\n  \"type2\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src2\": \"isolated color pixel s2 away from the surrounded area bottleneck\",\n  \"dst2\": \"\",\n  \"match_cond2\": \"\",\n  \"path2\": \"straight line to the edge of the grid, same as the radiate direction\",\n  \"trajectory2\": \"bg color\",\n  \"transform2\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"df9fd884\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3817\nmechanism=0.4690\nlexical=0.0139\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:draw_line, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
